<h2><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>2.
SNMP Communications Architecture<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

<p><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;color:#333333'>The Node.js
backend serves as a secure middleware layer responsible for handling
synchronous UDP polling from the target hardware limits. This guarantees the
frontend does not get bottlenecked making direct network requests.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<ul type=disc>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='color:#333333;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
     auto;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><b><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>Target
     SNMP Agent IP:</span></b><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'> </span><span class=code1><span
     style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>192.168.100.11</span></span><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'><o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='color:#333333;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
     auto;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><b><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>Target
     Port:</span></b><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:
     "Times New Roman"'> UDP Port </span><span class=code1><span
     style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>161</span></span><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>
     (Standard SNMP)<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='color:#333333;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
     auto;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><b><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>SNMP
     Version:</span></b><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'> v2c<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='color:#333333;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
     auto;mso-list:l4 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><b><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>Community
     String:</span></b><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'> </span><span class=code1><span
     style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>read</span></span><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>
     (Read-Only access) / </span><span class=code1><span style='font-size:10.0pt;
     mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>private</span></span><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>
     (Write access mapping)<o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ul>

<h3><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>Backend
Polling Algorithm &amp; Time Cycle<o:p></o:p></span></h3>

<p><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;color:#333333'>The system
establishes a controlled trickle-polling strategy to prevent overwhelming the
target SNMP agent. Instead of firing bulk requests which resulted in timeout
failures, the script fetches OIDs asynchronously one-by-one.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<ul type=disc>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='color:#333333;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
     auto;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><b><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>Backend
     Polling Cycle:</span></b><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'> The Node.js application
     executes a complete polling pipeline every <b>5000 milliseconds (5
     seconds)</b> using </span><span class=SpellE><span class=GramE><span
     class=code1><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>setInterval</span></span></span></span><span
     class=GramE><span class=code1><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:
     "Times New Roman"'>(</span></span></span><span class=SpellE><span
     class=code1><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>pollSnmpData</span></span></span><span
     class=code1><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>,
     5000)</span></span><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='color:#333333;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
     auto;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><b><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>Recursive
     Fetching Logic:</span></b><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'> Inside the cycle, OIDs are
     queried sequentially using a recursive function </span><span class=SpellE><span
     class=GramE><span class=code1><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:
     "Times New Roman"'>fetchNextSingleOid</span></span></span></span><span
     class=GramE><span class=code1><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:
     "Times New Roman"'>(</span></span></span><span class=code1><span
     style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>)</span></span><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>.
     This ensures the request for OID[x+1] only fires after the UDP response
     for OID[x] is successfully parsed or errors out natively after a 1000ms
     timeout window.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='color:#333333;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
     auto;mso-list:l2 level1 lfo2;tab-stops:list 36.0pt'><b><span
     style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>Frontend
     Polling Cycle:</span></b><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'> Concurrently, the <span
     class=SpellE>Javascript</span> dashboard UI fetches the cached JSON
     payload from the Node.js REST API (</span><span class=code1><span
     style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>/<span
     class=SpellE>api</span>/data</span></span><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>) every <b>1000 milliseconds (1
     second)</b> using </span><span class=SpellE><span class=GramE><span
     class=code1><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>setInterval</span></span></span></span><span
     class=GramE><span class=code1><span style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:
     "Times New Roman"'>(</span></span></span><span class=code1><span
     style='font-size:10.0pt;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>()
     =&gt; <span class=SpellE><span class=GramE>app.fetchData</span></span>(),
     1000)</span></span><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;
     mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'> to guarantee maximum
     responsiveness without initiating unnecessary network packets.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ul>

<h2><span style='font-family:"Calibri",sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:"Times New Roman"'>3.
Explicit OID Mappings Documented<o:p></o:p></span></h2>

